## Why This Is Asked
Tests production-grade RAG design across multilingual, heterogeneous corpora with multi-tenant isolation and performance constraints at scale.

## Key Concepts
- Hierarchical chunking (document → sections → paragraphs) with size optimization
- Multilingual embeddings and incremental refresh pipelines
- Vector DB partitioning with ACLs per tenant
- Two-stage retrieval with semantic search and cross-encoder reranking
- Freshness management, latency budgets (200-500ms), and comprehensive failover strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Implementation sketch for chunking and indexing
function chunkDocument(text, maxBytes = 4000) {
  const chunks = [];
  let current = '';

  // Split by paragraphs and respect semantic boundaries
  const paragraphs = text.split(/\n\s*\n/);

  for (const paragraph of paragraphs) {
    if (current.length + paragraph.length > maxBytes) {
      if (current) chunks.push(current.trim());
      current = paragraph;
    } else {
      current += (current ? '\n\n' : '') + paragraph;
    }
  }

  if (current) chunks.push(current.trim());
  return chunks;
}

// Tenant-aware retrieval
async function retrieveChunks(query, tenantId, limit = 5) {
  const embeddedQuery = await embedQuery(query);
  const results = await vectorStore.search({
    vector: embeddedQuery,
    filter: { tenantId },
    limit: limit * 2 // Get more for reranking
  });

  // Rerank with cross-encoder
  return await rerank(query, results).slice(0, limit);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Microsoft tests understanding of tokenization trade-offs and attention mechanisms in multilingual contexts - critical for products like Bing Chat and Azure AI services.

## Expected Answer
Strong candidates discuss: 1) Byte-Pair Encoding with language-specific merges, 2) Vocabulary size vs token count trade-offs, 3) Adding language ID tokens, 4) Attention modifications like language-aware positional encoding or cross-lingual attention heads.

## Code Example
```typescript
// Custom tokenizer with language-aware merges
class MultilingualTokenizer {
  vocabulary: Map<string, number>
  languageMerges: Map<string, string[]>

  tokenize(text: string, lang: string): number[] {
    const tokens = []
    const merges = this.languageMerges.get(lang) || []
    // Apply language-specific BPE merges
    return this.applyBPE(text, merges)
  }
}

// Language-aware attention modification
class LanguageAwareAttention {
  forward(x: Tensor, langIds: Tensor): Tensor {
    const attention = this.multiHeadAttention(x)
    const langBias = this.getLanguageBias(langIds)
    return attention + langBias
  }
}
```

